# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The context was ~2.95 GB, which is why every deploy transferred gigabytes and
# took minutes. Two causes:
#
#   1. .kilo/worktrees holds a full DUPLICATE CLONE of this repository (5.28 GB
#      of Clients/, Webserver/, Maps/). The bare `.kilo` entry did not reliably
#      exclude it, so it was uploaded on every build.
#   2. The 60-90 MB client installers under public/downloads and www/downloads
#      are artefacts, not source - they are rebuilt by tools/installer, and
#      uploading three copies of an 87 MB .exe dwarfs the actual code.
#
# Everything below is either a duplicate, a build artefact, or local-only state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Full duplicate clones of the repo (the single biggest offender).
.kilo
.kilo/
**/.kilo
**/.kilo/**
worktrees
**/worktrees/**

# Local editor / tool state.
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Runtime artefacts and logs.
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/*.tmp-*
run.log
run.err
g.err
**/authdigest_shm.*
**/httpd.pid

# Apache/PHP runtime dirs - not needed to build or run the Node services.
Webserver/bin/apache/logs
Webserver/bin/database

# Client installers: large binaries that the build does not consume. The server
# serves these from disk at runtime when present, so they are copied in
# separately by the deploy if they are wanted.
Webserver/http-db-bridge/public/downloads
Webserver/www/downloads

# Local-only data and workspaces.
workspace/saved_places
Uploads

# The 2013 web reference material (CSS/JS read while rebuilding the pages). It is
# ~103 MB and nothing at runtime reads it - the styles were copied into
# public/css/*.css. Kept in the repo for reference, excluded from the image.
Web-2013 CCS+JS

# NOTE: Maps/ and Clients/ are deliberately NOT ignored. gameMapResolver.js
# builds the game catalog from Maps/ at boot, and Clients/ is served to the game
# clients (AppSettings.xml, ClientSettings, the binaries), so both are required
# at runtime - ignoring either would break the site.

# Test fixtures and docs that do not ship.
tests
